    <monstor_v5:Applicant_projects>Face Mask Detection, Classification, and Segmentation | Python, OpenCV, PyTorch
∗ Developed a computer vision solution to classify and segment face masks in images using both handcrafted features and
deep learning models
∗ Implemented binary classification using machine learning classifiers (SVM, Neural Network) and a Convolutional Neural
Network (CNN) for mask detection.
∗ Performed region segmentation with traditional methods (thresholding, edge detection) and U-Net for mask segmentation,
evaluating performance with IoU and Dice score metrics
∗ Compared and analyzed the performance of machine learning classifiers, CNN, and U-Net on the mask detection and
segmentation tasks.
Predictive Model for Candidate Hiring Decisions | Python
∗ Developed a predictive model to determine whether a candidate would be hired based on attributes like assessment scores
and experience
∗ Applied machine learning algorithms, including Logistic Regression, Decision Trees, Random Forest, and Ensemble
methods, to predict hiring outcomes
∗ Evaluated the models’ performance and identified key factors influencing the hiring decision
∗ Fine-tuned model hyperparameters to improve accuracy and provide a more reliable hiring prediction system</monstor_v5:Applicant_projects>
